The main function of the EPS Session Management (ESM) sublayer, as described for the radio interface (LTE-Uu), is **to support the EPS bearer context handling in the UE and in the MME**.

This includes:
- The activation, deactivation, and modification of EPS bearer contexts;
- Handling requests from the UE for resources (such as IP connectivity to a PDN or dedicated bearer resources);
- Transporting user data via the control plane between the UE and the MME.

Each EPS bearer context represents an EPS bearer between the UE and a Packet Data Network Gateway (PDN-GW), and can be either a default or dedicated bearer context. These contexts may remain activated even when underlying radio and S1 bearers are temporarily released.
